  "summary": "New preprints automate Patch-seq, atlas-based neuron identification, glomerulus mapping and cross-modality image registration for single-cell spatial analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is scaling quantitative cell characterization by coupling automation with multimodal registration. Patch-seq work shows that detergent-cleaned reusable pipettes, robotic nucleus extraction and sonication preserve electrophysiology and transcriptomic yield. In C. elegans, probabilistic atlases from near-wild-type strains reach 86.3% top-1 variability-aware neuron identification. Whole-bulb light-sheet expansion microscopy with automated segmentation quantifies thousands of glomeruli in intact mouse olfactory bulbs. SCOUBI infers axon-dendrite interfaces from extrasomatic transcripts in spatial transcriptomics. A parallel strand integrates imaging modalities: MeXalign coregisters LA-ICP-TOFMS and immunofluorescence via segmentation masks, and FluoMALDI links fluorescence-defined genes, proteins and organelles to spatial lipid composition. Disease- and glia-focused tools add 3D readouts: PASTA resolves amyloid-beta plaque heterogeneity and microglial contacts, and PolyMorph3D quantifies microglia morphology with multi-marker colocalization. Stitched montage cryo-ET of lamellipodial actin is methodologically related but lies outside neural tissue.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
